{% block subheader %}
<p class="intro">This page outlines my work in ethnography and creative practice, spanning anthropology, science and technology studies (STS), multimodal inventions, and urban research, all unified by a focus on fragments—tiny traces that reflect everyday life's hidden complexity. For me, ethnography is more than description; it's a curatorial and experimental process that uses fieldnotes, illustrations, and workshops to capture, document, and reimagine. My research is both analytical and imaginative. My ethnographic focus is on understanding life in fragmented, more-than-human worlds through residues, urban infrastructure, multispecies encounters, and speculative archives.</p>
